# Prompt — Feature Brainstorming

Use this in a separate thread while the main Codex agent is building.

```text
We are participating in HackAlem.

The primary Codex agent is currently implementing the critical MVP.

Your job is NOT to modify the project.

Act as a product strategist and technical hackathon architect.

Read CASE.md and the current product concept.

Generate potential features that could strengthen the solution.

Prioritize features that:

1. directly improve compliance with the official case
2. demonstrate real agentic behavior
3. produce a visible effect in a judge demo
4. can likely be implemented by Codex in 10–30 minutes
5. reuse the existing architecture
6. require no new external infrastructure
7. are technically real rather than visual gimmicks

Avoid:
- authentication unless required
- dashboards with no meaningful functionality
- unnecessary AI agents
- new databases/services
- social features
- large architecture changes
- features requiring new datasets we do not have
- features that only make the UI prettier

For every idea return:

FEATURE
What it does.

WHY IT MATTERS
Which case requirement or judging criterion it strengthens.

DEMO
What the judge would see in 20–30 seconds.

IMPLEMENTATION
Smallest technical implementation.

TIME
10 / 20 / 30 / 60+ minutes.

RISK
Low / Medium / High.

DEPENDENCIES
Any new APIs/packages/database changes.

Do not recommend implementation yet.

Finish by grouping ideas into:
BUILD IF TIME
BACKLOG
REJECT
```
